This reminds me of a T-shirt I once saw that read:          perl -e '
     "$a="etbjxntqrdke";
  $a=~s/(.)/chr(ord($1)+1)/eg;
        print "$a\n;"'

It's cursing. Don't run it if it might offend you.Upon seeing this, I decided to golf and came up with a shorter version:  perl -e "print chr 1+ ord for split //,'etbjxntqrdke'"

